          "__seccion_4__": "Original price was $1,200 in 1935",
          "__seccion_5__": "The GP was originally designated the Model C, the name was changed due to a similarity to the existing D, plus the \"General Purpose\" name was a marketing ploy to keep in line with International's new \"Farmall\". The GP was designed as a row crop tractor, with the fixed front axle straddling three rows. Several versions of the GP were made. The \"wide tread\" GPWT has a 76-inch rear axle and a tricycle front. The GP-P was a modified GPWT with a 68-inch rear axle, for use in potato fields. The GPO was lowered and had fenders for orchard work. Twenty-four GPO tractors were converted into crawlers by Lindeman."
